  "body": "What happens: outside Area mode (Boundary operations), law (b) in `crates/sim/src/verify/section.rs` reads an arc move only at its chord joints (`segments`, about lines 200-203; `laws.rs` 96-108). Arcs get no whole-move reading there (`wall_gouge` skips them, about line 113). A sharp wall or island corner that falls between two joints is never measured against the cutter.\n\nEvidence (high-tier review of PR #839, https://github.com/NeoTech/Camcraft/pull/839#pullrequestreview-5864925404): on main's reading, a 4 mm cutter on an r 200 arc sweeping 0.048 rad passes a 0.29 mm gouge when the corner sits midway between two joints. PR #839 quarters the chord tolerance, which makes the worst case about 4x smaller, but the reading stays point-sampled. Area mode is not affected (it convicts under both readings).\n\nExpected: an arc move in Boundary mode is judged along its whole length against wall edges and corners (closest distance from the corner to the arc, not to sampled points), so the verdict does not depend on where the joints land.\n\nNot part of #839: its own blocker (reading the union of old and new joints so no old conviction is lost) is fixed on that PR. This issue is the remaining gap.\n\nDone means: a test places a sharp corner midway between an arc's joints at a clearance past the floor and gets a gouge; the same case just inside the floor stays clean; Area-mode verdicts are unchanged.\n",
